  "notes": "Boot a No Fear ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released); the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM BOOKKEEPING TOTALS CLEARED loop with Escape (5), press Enter twice (game identification, then MAIN MENU), Up twice to T. TESTS and Enter to open the test menu at T.1 SWITCH EDGES. Run it with PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled (--handle-mechanics 0), as the known-working table does; nfGameData declares none. Open T.18 UNDERGROUND TROUGH TEST in MANUAL mode and set the four trough switches the test shows (38, 37, 42, 41) to public 1 and back one at a time. Then load the ball trough (32-35 at public 1), switch to AUTOMATIC with Enter and walk one ball through the cycle the manual describes: wait for the trough eject, release trough 4 and close the shooter lane, wait for the auto plunger, then pass the left and center trough entrances and right popper 2 and hold right popper 1 until the ROM fires the right popper. The switch levels are host stimuli; the outputs are the ROM's.",
